<http://asu.edu/semantics/SUDOKN/NAICSClassifier> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#Class> .
<http://asu.edu/semantics/SUDOKN/NAICSClassifier> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The SUDOKN class for NAICS classifiers, asserted as a second type on the 13 NAICS Industry Classification nodes to align this graph with the SUDOKN manufacturing graph. Read the codes through md:naicsCode." .
<http://asu.edu/semantics/SUDOKN/NAICSClassifier> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "NAICS Classifier (SUDOKN)" .
<http://asu.edu/semantics/SUDOKN/hasNAICSClassifier> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#Property> .
<http://asu.edu/semantics/SUDOKN/hasNAICSClassifier> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The SUDOKN property linking a manufacturer to a NAICS industry. It repeats the manufacturer links of md:hasNAICSClassification (the same 13,972 triples) in SUDOKN and IOF terms. The assignments are inferred by the knowledge graph's crosswalk and are not supplied by FDA." .
<http://asu.edu/semantics/SUDOKN/hasNAICSClassifier> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "has NAICS classifier (SUDOKN)" .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/AccessGUDIDRecord> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#Class> .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/AccessGUDIDRecord> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A device record from AccessGUDID, the public view of the Global Unique Device Identification Database. A subclass of FDA Data Record. Declared in the schema but not populated in the current release." .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/AccessGUDIDRecord> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "AccessGUDID / UDI Record" .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/AdverseEventReport> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#Class> .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/AdverseEventReport> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The parent class of device adverse-event report classes, including MAUDE and MedSun reports. A subclass of FDA Data Record. Declared in the schema but not populated in the current release." .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/AdverseEventReport> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Adverse Event Report" .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/Analyte> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#Class> .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/Analyte> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A substance or constituent measured by a diagnostic test. Declared in the schema but not populated in the current release." .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/Analyte> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Analyte" .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/ApprovalPathway> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#Class> .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/ApprovalPathway> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The regulatory pathway by which a device reached the market, such as 510(k), PMA, De Novo, or HDE. Declared in the schema but not populated in the current release." .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/ApprovalPathway> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Approval Pathway" .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/CFRTitle21Section> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#Class> .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/CFRTitle21Section> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A section of Title 21 of the Code of Federal Regulations, with its authority and full regulatory text." .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/CFRTitle21Section> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "21 CFR Section" .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/CLIARecord> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#Class> .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/CLIARecord> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A laboratory test system record under the Clinical Laboratory Improvement Amendments. A subclass of FDA Data Record. Declared in the schema but not populated in the current release." .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/CLIARecord> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "CLIA Laboratory Test System Record" .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/CLIAWaivedRecord> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#Class> .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/CLIAWaivedRecord> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A record of an analyte waived from routine CLIA oversight. A subclass of FDA Data Record. Declared in the schema but not populated in the current release." .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/CLIAWaivedRecord> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "CLIA Waived Analyte Record" .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/CfrPart> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#Class> .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/CfrPart> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A part of Title 21 of the Code of Federal Regulations that groups related sections." .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/CfrPart> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "21 CFR Part" .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/CliaWaivedAnalyte> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#Class> .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/CliaWaivedAnalyte> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "An analyte whose test is waived from routine regulatory oversight under the Clinical Laboratory Improvement Amendments." .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/CliaWaivedAnalyte> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "CLIA Waived Analyte" .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/Component> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#Class> .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/Component> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A component of a medical device. A subclass of Device Component. Declared in the schema but not populated in the current release." .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/Component> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Component" .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/Dataset> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#Class> .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/Dataset> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "An FDA source dataset that records in the graph were extracted from. Declared in the schema but not populated in the current release." .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/Dataset> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "FDA Source Dataset" .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/DeNovoRecord> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#Class> .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/DeNovoRecord> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A De Novo classification request granting marketing authorization to a novel low-to-moderate risk device that has no valid predicate. A subclass of Regulatory Submission." .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/DeNovoRecord> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "De Novo Authorization" .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/DesignChange> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#Class> .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/DesignChange> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A change to a device design; the parent class of PMA supplements. Declared in the schema but not populated in the current release." .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/DesignChange> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Design Change" .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/DeviceComponent> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#Class> .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/DeviceComponent> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The parent class for device components. Declared in the schema but not populated in the current release." .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/DeviceComponent> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Device Component" .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/DeviceFDARecord> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#Class> .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/DeviceFDARecord> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "An entry in the Devices@FDA catalog, linking a marketed device to the submission and pathway under which it reached the market." .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/DeviceFDARecord> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Devices@FDA Catalog Record" .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/DeviceIdentifier> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#Class> .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/DeviceIdentifier> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The device identifier portion of a Unique Device Identification code. Declared in the schema but not populated in the current release." .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/DeviceIdentifier> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Device Identifier (UDI)" .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/DeviceListing> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#Class> .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/DeviceListing> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A device listing filed by a registered establishment. A subclass of FDA Data Record. Declared in the schema but not populated in the current release." .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/DeviceListing> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "FDA Device Listing" .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/DeviceMaterial> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#Class> .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/DeviceMaterial> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The parent class for device materials. Declared in the schema but not populated in the current release." .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/DeviceMaterial> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Device Material" .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/DeviceProblem> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#Class> .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/DeviceProblem> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A device problem code reported on MDRs for a TPLC product code, with its report and event counts." .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/DeviceProblem> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Device Problem" .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/DevicesFDARecord> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#Class> .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/DevicesFDARecord> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The declared class for Devices@FDA catalog entries. A subclass of FDA Data Record. Declared in the schema but not populated in the current release." .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/DevicesFDARecord> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Devices@FDA Catalog Record (declared)" .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/FDADataRecord> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#Class> .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/FDADataRecord> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The root class for records extracted from an FDA source dataset; all dataset-specific record classes are subclasses of it. Declared in the schema but not populated in the current release." .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/FDADataRecord> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "FDA Data Record" .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/Facility> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#Class> .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/Facility> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "An FDA-registered establishment whose registration address has been geocoded. A subclass of FDA Registration and Listing Record: each of the 9,120 facilities is also typed md:RegistrationListingRecord and geo:Feature, keeps all registration properties, and adds a point geometry, latitude and longitude, a normalized address, and the geocoder's source and confidence. Almost all are U.S. addresses; the other 16,012 registration records have no coordinates. Reach the NAICS industry of a facility through md:hasManufacturer and md:hasNAICSClassification (3,452 facilities have one)." .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/Facility> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Geocoded Facility" .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/GMDNTerm> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#Class> .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/GMDNTerm> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A Global Medical Device Nomenclature term describing a generic device group. Declared in the schema but not populated in the current release." .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/GMDNTerm> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "GMDN Term" .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/HDERecord> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#Class> .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/HDERecord> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The declared record class for Humanitarian Device Exemptions. A subclass of Regulatory Submission. Declared in the schema but not populated in the current release." .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/HDERecord> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Humanitarian Device Exemption Record" .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/HumanitarianDeviceExemption> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#Class> .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/HumanitarianDeviceExemption> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A Humanitarian Device Exemption record, covering a device intended to treat or diagnose a condition affecting a small patient population." .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/HumanitarianDeviceExemption> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Humanitarian Device Exemption" .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/IVDHomeUseTest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#Class> .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/IVDHomeUseTest> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "An in vitro diagnostic test cleared or approved for home (over-the-counter) use." .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/IVDHomeUseTest> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "IVD Home-Use Test" .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/IVDRecord> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#Class> .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/IVDRecord> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The declared class for in vitro diagnostic home-use test records. A subclass of FDA Data Record. Declared in the schema but not populated in the current release." .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/IVDRecord> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "IVD Home-Use Test Record" .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/K510Record> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#Class> .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/K510Record> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A premarket notification submission under section 510(k), by which a device is cleared for market on the basis of substantial equivalence to a legally marketed predicate device. A subclass of Regulatory Submission." .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/K510Record> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "510(k) Submission" .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/MAUDEReport> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#Class> .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/MAUDEReport> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A Medical Device Report (MDR) from the FDA Manufacturer and User Facility Device Experience (MAUDE) system, describing a suspected device-associated death, serious injury, or malfunction. A subclass of Adverse Event Report." .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/MAUDEReport> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "MAUDE Adverse Event Report" .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/MDRStatistic> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#Class> .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/MDRStatistic> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A yearly count of medical device reports and events for a TPLC product code." .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/MDRStatistic> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "MDR Statistic" .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/MammographyFacility> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#Class> .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/MammographyFacility> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A mammography facility certified under the Mammography Quality Standards Act. A subclass of FDA Data Record." .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/MammographyFacility> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "MQSA Certified Mammography Facility" .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/Manufacturer> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#Class> .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/Manufacturer> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A firm or establishment named on an FDA record, identified where possible by its FDA Establishment Identifier (FEI). The 10,432 manufacturers that carry a NAICS classification are also typed iof:Manufacturer." .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/Manufacturer> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Manufacturer" .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/Material> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#Class> .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/Material> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A material a device is made from. A subclass of Device Material. Declared in the schema but not populated in the current release." .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/Material> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Material" .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/MedSunReport> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#Class> .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/MedSunReport> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A report from MedSun, the Medical Product Safety Network of sentinel reporting facilities. A subclass of Adverse Event Report. Declared in the schema but not populated in the current release." .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/MedSunReport> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "MedSun Safety Report" .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/MedicalDevice> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#Class> .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/MedicalDevice> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A medical device, the hub entity that FDA records about the same product are attached to." .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/MedicalDevice> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Medical Device" .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/NAICSClassification> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#Class> .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/NAICSClassification> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A North American Industry Classification System (NAICS) industry, with its six-digit code in md:naicsCode, the NAICS version in md:naicsVersion, and the industry title in rdfs:label. The graph holds 13 NAICS 2022 industries (e.g., 339112 Surgical and Medical Instrument Manufacturing), assigned to manufacturers and FDA product codes by the knowledge graph's own crosswalk, not by FDA. The same nodes are also typed sud:NAICSClassifier." .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/NAICSClassification> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "NAICS Industry Classification" .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/PMAChangeMemo> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#Class> .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/PMAChangeMemo> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A supplement to an approved PMA covering a change to the device, its manufacturing, or its labeling. A subclass of Design Change." .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/PMAChangeMemo> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "PMA Supplement" .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/PMARecord> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#Class> .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/PMARecord> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A Premarket Approval application, the FDA scientific and regulatory review pathway required for Class III devices. A subclass of Regulatory Submission." .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/PMARecord> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "PMA Submission" .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/PatientOutcome> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#Class> .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/PatientOutcome> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A patient outcome code reported on MDRs for a TPLC product code, with its report and event counts." .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/PatientOutcome> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Patient Outcome" .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/Postmarket522Study> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#Class> .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/Postmarket522Study> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A postmarket surveillance study ordered under section 522 of the Federal Food, Drug, and Cosmetic Act. A subclass of FDA Data Record." .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/Postmarket522Study> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "522 Postmarket Surveillance Study" .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/ProductClassificationRecord> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#Class> .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/ProductClassificationRecord> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The FDA classification record for a product code, giving its device class, regulation, review panel, and regulatory flags. A subclass of FDA Data Record. Its nodes (IRIs ending productcode/<code>) are separate from the FDA Product Code nodes (IRIs ending product-code/<code>); only 443 nodes carry both types, so join the two on the md:productCode literal. 1,589 of the 7,071 records carry a NAICS industry through md:hasNAICSClassification." .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/ProductClassificationRecord> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "FDA Product Classification Record" .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/ProductCode> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#Class> .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/ProductCode> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A three-letter FDA product code identifying a device type; the key most FDA device datasets join on. Its nodes (IRIs ending product-code/<code>) are separate from the FDA Product Classification Record nodes (IRIs ending productcode/<code>); only 443 nodes carry both types, so join the two on the md:productCode literal." .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/ProductCode> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "FDA Product Code" .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/ProductCodeNAICSMapping> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#Class> .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/ProductCodeNAICSMapping> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A crosswalk assertion that assigns a NAICS industry to an FDA product code, recording the method, source, confidence, review status, and justification of the assignment. The mappings are inferred by the knowledge graph's builders and are not supplied by FDA." .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/ProductCodeNAICSMapping> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Product Code to NAICS Mapping" .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/ProvenanceRecord> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#Class> .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/ProvenanceRecord> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "An extraction audit record describing how and when data was harvested. Declared in the schema but not populated in the current release." .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/ProvenanceRecord> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Provenance Record" .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/Recall> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#Class> .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/Recall> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A recall event summarised on a TPLC product-code record, giving its class and date." .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/Recall> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Recall" .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/RecallRecord> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#Class> .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/RecallRecord> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A device recall enforcement record from the openFDA recall dataset, with the recalling firm, reason, classification, and distribution. A subclass of FDA Data Record." .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/RecallRecord> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Device Recall Record" .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/RecognizedConsensusStandard> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#Class> .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/RecognizedConsensusStandard> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A voluntary consensus standard recognized by FDA for use in device premarket submissions." .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/RecognizedConsensusStandard> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Recognized Consensus Standard" .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/RecognizedStandard> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#Class> .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/RecognizedStandard> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The declared class for FDA-recognized voluntary consensus standards. A subclass of FDA Data Record. Declared in the schema but not populated in the current release." .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/RecognizedStandard> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "FDA Recognized Consensus Standard" .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/RegistrationListingRecord> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#Class> .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/RegistrationListingRecord> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "An establishment registration and device listing record, giving the registered facility, its status, and its registration number. A subclass of FDA Data Record. The 9,120 records with a geocoded address are also typed md:Facility." .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/RegistrationListingRecord> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "FDA Registration and Listing Record" .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/RegulationNumber> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#Class> .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/RegulationNumber> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A 21 CFR regulation number under which a device type is classified." .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/RegulationNumber> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Regulation Number" .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/RegulatorySubmission> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#Class> .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/RegulatorySubmission> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A premarket submission to FDA; the parent class of the 510(k), PMA, De Novo, and HDE record classes. A subclass of FDA Data Record. Declared in the schema but not populated in the current release." .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/RegulatorySubmission> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Regulatory Submission" .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/SafetyReport> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#Class> .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/SafetyReport> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A device safety report; a parent class for adverse-event reporting sources. A subclass of Adverse Event Report. Declared in the schema but not populated in the current release." .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/SafetyReport> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Safety Report" .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/SafetySignal> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#Class> .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/SafetySignal> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A derived safety signal identified from postmarket data. Declared in the schema but not populated in the current release." .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/SafetySignal> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Safety Signal" .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/SoftwareFeature> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#Class> .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/SoftwareFeature> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A software feature or function of a device. Declared in the schema but not populated in the current release." .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/SoftwareFeature> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Software Feature" .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/SourceRecord> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#Class> .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/SourceRecord> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The raw FDA record a graph entity was derived from. Declared in the schema but not populated in the current release." .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/SourceRecord> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Source Record" .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/Specialty> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#Class> .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/Specialty> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A laboratory specialty or subspecialty recognized under CLIA. Declared in the schema but not populated in the current release." .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/Specialty> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "CLIA Laboratory Specialty" .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/TPLCRecord> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#Class> .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/TPLCRecord> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A Total Product Life Cycle record, aggregating device problems, patient outcomes, MDR trends, and recalls for one FDA product code. A subclass of FDA Data Record." .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/TPLCRecord> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "TPLC Device Record" .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/TestSystem> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#Class> .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/TestSystem> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A test system, assay, or instrument categorised under CLIA. Declared in the schema but not populated in the current release." .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/TestSystem> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "CLIA Test System" .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/UDIIdentifier> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#Class> .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/UDIIdentifier> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "One entry from the AccessGUDID identifiers list; may be a primary DI, package DI, or unit-of-use DI. Declared in the schema but not populated in the current release." .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/UDIIdentifier> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "UDI Identifier" .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/XRayAssemblerRecord> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#Class> .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/XRayAssemblerRecord> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The declared class for FDA x-ray assembler reports. A subclass of FDA Data Record. Declared in the schema but not populated in the current release." .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/XRayAssemblerRecord> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "FDA X-Ray Assembler Record" .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/XrayAssemblerRecord> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#Class> .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/XrayAssemblerRecord> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "An FDA x-ray assembler report recording the installation of diagnostic x-ray equipment at a named site." .
<http://medicaldevice.com/ontology/XrayAssemblerRecord> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "X-Ray Assembler Record" .
